# Game art is always included, even when an enclosing directory's ignore rules exclude
# images. `railway up` honours .gitignore, and without these negations the assets once
# never reached the Railway build context and the web export failed with
# "Failed loading resource: res://Assets/background.jpg".
#
# These are deliberately STRUCTURAL, not a list of the files that exist today. An enumerated
# form (!Assets/*.png) misses any image in a subfolder or outside Assets/, and `!` does not
# cross a `/`. Adding Assets/particles/spark.png would then fail on Railway and pass locally,
# which is the exact incident this file exists to prevent.
!**/*.png
!**/*.jpg
!**/*.jpeg
!**/*.gif
!**/*.svg
!**/*.webp

# Every hidden folder at the root (tool caches, editor settings) stays out,
# except .github/, where workflows live. Build output too. Never committed,
# never uploaded.
/.*/
!/.github/
build/
export_presets.cfg

# The single-player build this replaced. Kept for reference, never shipped:
# `railway up` honours this file, so anything here stays out of the upload.
archives/
node_modules/

# The brand kit. Reference material, not shipped: the mark lives in
# brand/ and tools/build-brand.py renders it. `railway up` honours this file, so
# without the line the zip and the design canvas ride into every deploy.
# Listed BEFORE the screenshots note for the same reason it gives: an excluded
# directory is never descended into, so the !**/*.png negations above cannot
# rescue anything inside it, which is exactly what we want here.
Branding/

# 11 MB of proof screenshots. .dockerignore already keeps them out of the image,
# but `railway up` honours THIS file, so without the line they were uploaded on
# every single deploy for nothing. Listed after the image negations on purpose:
# an excluded directory is never descended into, so `!**/*.png` cannot rescue it.
verification/

# Secrets. This folder is a git repository of its own, so no enclosing directory's
# `.env` rule reaches it: without these lines a local .env would commit.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Python caches from tools/, a local venv, and logs from local runs.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
*.log

# Local notes. Never published, never uploaded.
md files/

# OS clutter.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
